4
00:02:44,240 --> 00:02:48,160
THE FIRST CUP OF OSMANTHUS MILK

5
00:02:49,560 --> 00:02:51,920
This bag is too expensive.
I can't take it.

6
00:02:54,600 --> 00:02:55,720
So you won't take the bag,

7
00:02:56,560 --> 00:02:58,120
but you want to talk about feelings?

8
00:03:08,280 --> 00:03:09,400
Take the bag.

9
00:03:10,280 --> 00:03:11,120
Give me a loaf of bread.

10
00:03:13,160 --> 00:03:14,920
You bought all those loaves.

11
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:16,120
Can't I take one?

12
00:03:18,600 --> 00:03:21,080
MORE BEAUTY IN LIFE

13
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:37,120
I'll get going, then.

14
00:03:48,720 --> 00:03:53,040
So he just gave you a bag
and said nothing more?

15
00:03:55,600 --> 00:03:56,720
Don't overthink it.

16
00:03:57,240 --> 00:03:58,800
Men usually aren't good with words.

17
00:03:59,400 --> 00:04:02,600
Maybe he just wanted to give you a bag.

18
00:04:05,880 --> 00:04:09,960
But I saw a lot of gift boxes
in his trunk.

19
00:04:10,560 --> 00:04:14,040
Maybe he keeps them handy
to buy people's silence.

20
00:04:16,720 --> 00:04:18,720
For a payoff this expensive,

21
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:22,680
I'll definitely keep
his little mistake a secret.

22
00:04:25,120 --> 00:04:27,400
Tao, could you have misunderstood him?

23
00:04:30,480 --> 00:04:31,480
I don't know.

24
00:04:32,400 --> 00:04:33,960
And I don't want to know.

25
00:04:36,080 --> 00:04:38,120
I don't want anything that isn't mine.

26
00:04:42,720 --> 00:04:43,680
Tao.

27
00:04:46,280 --> 00:04:48,920
You may not be sure yet,

28
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:50,840
and you'd deny it if I said it.

29
00:04:51,560 --> 00:04:54,560
But Tao, the truth is,

30
00:04:54,640 --> 00:04:55,600
you're not someone who fools around.

31
00:04:56,400 --> 00:05:00,000
You've fallen for him, haven't you?

32
00:05:00,560 --> 00:05:02,240
Whether I like him doesn't matter.

33
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:05,240
I just feel stupid.

34
00:05:06,120 --> 00:05:08,880
Stupid enough to have
unrealistic fantasies about him.

35
00:05:21,920 --> 00:05:23,800
The misattribution of arousal theory says

36
00:05:25,800 --> 00:05:28,400
that what we feel when we're in danger

37
00:05:30,960 --> 00:05:32,120
isn't necessarily love.

38
00:05:37,480 --> 00:05:40,800
I'll still see him at work every day.

39
00:05:40,880 --> 00:05:42,680
I feel awkward just thinking about it.

40
00:05:43,320 --> 00:05:44,760
Shang Zhitao,

41
00:05:44,840 --> 00:05:48,360
you could become
an industry leader someday.

42
00:05:48,440 --> 00:05:50,200
Why let this bother you?

43
00:05:50,280 --> 00:05:51,480
Someday,

44
00:05:51,560 --> 00:05:53,960
when you make hundreds,
even thousands of times more,

45
00:05:54,040 --> 00:05:56,240
you can buy me full-price bread.

46
00:05:58,160 --> 00:05:59,600
I'll buy you the most expensive kind.

47
00:05:59,680 --> 00:06:01,280
- No discounted stuff.
- You'd better.

48
00:06:18,200 --> 00:06:20,800
HOW TO KEEP YOUR DISTANCE FROM YOUR BOSS

49
00:06:26,440 --> 00:06:27,360
KEEP BOUNDARIES CLEAR
FOLLOW THE CHAIN OF COMMAND

50
00:06:27,440 --> 00:06:28,320
USE DISCRETION WHEN REPORTING

51
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:30,160
ADULTS DON'T NEED EVERYTHING SPELLED OUT

52
00:06:31,080 --> 00:06:33,840
PRETEND NOTHING HAPPENED
SOMETIMES YOU GROW UP OVERNIGHT

53
00:06:58,680 --> 00:07:00,240
In the adult world,

54
00:07:01,280 --> 00:07:03,960
some things don't need to be spelled out

55
00:07:05,360 --> 00:07:06,920
or asked about.

56
00:07:08,280 --> 00:07:09,520
Shang Zhitao,

57
00:07:10,400 --> 00:07:13,920
you need to grow up fast.

58
00:07:41,240 --> 00:07:43,440
Come on. Try my cooking.

59
00:07:43,520 --> 00:07:46,360
You need fuel to fight monsters
and level up.

60
00:07:46,440 --> 00:07:48,040
- Reporting.
- Go ahead.

61
00:07:48,120 --> 00:07:49,600
I applied for a transfer.

62
00:07:49,680 --> 00:07:50,520
Really?

63
00:07:50,600 --> 00:07:53,040
Over the weekend, I talked to HR.

64
00:07:53,120 --> 00:07:53,960
They agreed.

65
00:07:54,920 --> 00:07:56,880
So you're leaving
Luan Nian's team for good?

66
00:07:58,080 --> 00:07:59,360
I've made up my mind.

67
00:07:59,440 --> 00:08:02,560
I really like this job.
I don't want to give it up.

68
00:08:02,640 --> 00:08:04,960
But what happened between us has happened.

69
00:08:05,040 --> 00:08:06,440
I can't change it.

70
00:08:07,080 --> 00:08:11,560
I think the best thing for both of us
is to draw a clear line.

71
00:08:13,920 --> 00:08:15,280
Tao, honestly,

72
00:08:15,360 --> 00:08:16,880
what happened between you two
is only natural.

73
00:08:16,960 --> 00:08:18,800
Don't put so much pressure on yourself.

74
00:08:19,480 --> 00:08:22,320
Didn't you say that when it comes to love,

75
00:08:22,400 --> 00:08:23,840
the first one to cave in loses?

76
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:24,920
Fair point.

77
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:27,400
I may be a little timid
and not brave enough,

78
00:08:27,480 --> 00:08:29,960
but I know I can handle this.

79
00:08:30,040 --> 00:08:31,840
I believe you can too.

80
00:08:31,920 --> 00:08:34,559
And it'll show him
you don't let feelings control you.

81
00:08:35,280 --> 00:08:36,120
Exactly.

82
00:08:37,440 --> 00:08:38,360
Let's eat.

83
00:08:51,040 --> 00:08:52,280
Busy?

84
00:08:55,120 --> 00:08:56,000
What's up?

85
00:08:57,280 --> 00:08:58,200
Nothing major.

86
00:08:58,280 --> 00:09:00,760
I just received a transfer request.

87
00:09:00,840 --> 00:09:03,680
It's from someone on your team,
so I came to ask about her.

88
00:09:03,760 --> 00:09:04,840
Who?

89
00:09:05,680 --> 00:09:08,880
Her name is Shang Zhitao.

90
00:09:15,320 --> 00:09:17,960
Shang Zhitao applied for a transfer?

91
00:09:18,040 --> 00:09:19,960
Everyone wants to move up.

92
00:09:20,840 --> 00:09:22,360
Tracy just forwarded me
her transfer request.

93
00:09:23,680 --> 00:09:24,920
What's she like?

94
00:09:26,480 --> 00:09:27,920
I don't have time to vet her for you.

95
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:31,640
You think that little of her?

96
00:09:32,680 --> 00:09:34,120
Not one good word?

97
00:09:35,920 --> 00:09:37,200
Fine. Got it.

98
00:09:37,840 --> 00:09:38,680
Then I don't want her.

99
00:09:40,360 --> 00:09:41,240
Wait.

100
00:09:49,880 --> 00:09:51,040
She's not exactly a natural.

101
00:09:53,120 --> 00:09:54,960
I can tell.

102
00:09:55,040 --> 00:09:57,200
But by your standards,

103
00:09:57,280 --> 00:09:59,280
there are probably only a handful
in the entire industry.

104
00:09:59,360 --> 00:10:00,640
What else?

105
00:10:03,280 --> 00:10:04,560
She's modest and never takes credit.

106
00:10:05,720 --> 00:10:06,680
She's patient.

107
00:10:07,280 --> 00:10:08,200
She never complains.

108
00:10:09,640 --> 00:10:10,920
She's persistent and hardworking.

109
00:10:12,880 --> 00:10:15,080
Sometimes she seems too willing
to put up with things,

110
00:10:15,840 --> 00:10:16,920
but she's ambitious.

111
00:10:21,120 --> 00:10:24,120
That's a pretty fair assessment.

112
00:10:25,160 --> 00:10:28,240
It's a shame she didn't stay on your team.

113
00:10:29,600 --> 00:10:30,560
Tracy,

114
00:10:30,640 --> 00:10:34,040
I'll approve Shang Zhitao's
transfer request.

115
00:10:35,200 --> 00:10:36,720
Put her in an account executive role.

116
00:10:36,800 --> 00:10:37,880
Have her start next Monday.

117
00:10:43,800 --> 00:10:44,840
Sorry to lose her?

118
00:10:45,520 --> 00:10:46,360
I don't care.

119
00:10:53,400 --> 00:10:54,440
Thanks.

120
00:11:13,920 --> 00:11:15,800
SHANG ZHITAO

121
00:11:57,520 --> 00:11:58,600
You're here early.

122
00:11:59,960 --> 00:12:01,000
Morning, Luke.

123
00:12:04,200 --> 00:12:05,520
Why did you apply for a transfer?

124
00:12:08,080 --> 00:12:09,600
I wanted a change of environment.

125
00:12:10,600 --> 00:12:12,520
Are you that eager to draw
a line between us?

126
00:12:14,520 --> 00:12:17,000
Luke, don't get the wrong idea.

127
00:12:17,080 --> 00:12:19,680
There was no other reason
for the transfer.

128
00:12:19,760 --> 00:12:22,560
It's just part of my career plan.

129
00:12:30,880 --> 00:12:32,280
Why aren't you using the bag I gave you?

130
00:12:39,160 --> 00:12:40,280
Don't worry.

131
00:12:41,440 --> 00:12:42,680
I accepted the bag.

132
00:12:43,480 --> 00:12:44,320
I'll keep your secret.

133
00:12:57,280 --> 00:12:59,680
Do you think you can only
get promoted on Alex's team?

134
00:13:01,600 --> 00:13:04,400
Whatever work I'm given,
I'll give it my all.

135
00:13:04,920 --> 00:13:07,080
Whether I get promoted is my own business.

136
00:13:07,920 --> 00:13:09,160
You can judge me by my work.

137
00:13:32,600 --> 00:13:34,040
Shang Zhitao, have you lost your mind?

138
00:13:34,120 --> 00:13:34,960
Lumi.

139
00:13:36,520 --> 00:13:39,800
Luke may have a sharp tongue,
but he's got clout.

140
00:13:39,880 --> 00:13:41,600
He was just starting to warm to you.

141
00:13:41,680 --> 00:13:43,520
This is when you should
be sticking close to him.

142
00:13:43,600 --> 00:13:45,360
So why… why did you run off instead?

143
00:13:46,600 --> 00:13:49,240
I don't meet his standards anyway.

144
00:13:49,320 --> 00:13:52,200
To him, I'm hardly worth mentioning.

145
00:13:54,080 --> 00:13:55,320
Did that stubborn mule chew you out again?

146
00:13:56,960 --> 00:13:59,920
Don't let a couple of harsh words
get to you.

147
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:00,840
Think about it.

148
00:14:01,480 --> 00:14:03,840
In Guangzhou, when that jerk tried
to force drinks on you,

149
00:14:03,920 --> 00:14:05,240
didn't Luke step in for you?

150
00:14:06,320 --> 00:14:08,160
When the shoot got hit by that downpour,

151
00:14:08,240 --> 00:14:09,760
didn't he go rescue you?

152
00:14:10,480 --> 00:14:11,800
After all that,

153
00:14:11,880 --> 00:14:13,840
even if he's a crooked old tree,

154
00:14:13,920 --> 00:14:15,680
at least he can shelter you
from the storm.

155
00:14:16,280 --> 00:14:17,400
But working with Alex?

156
00:14:17,480 --> 00:14:20,600
He's just a plastic potted plant.
All looks and no use.

157
00:14:21,360 --> 00:14:22,640
Meeting in the conference room.

158
00:14:27,960 --> 00:14:28,920
I've got a meeting.

159
00:14:33,360 --> 00:14:35,280
Well, look at that.

160
00:14:37,920 --> 00:14:38,880
Boss,

161
00:14:39,480 --> 00:14:41,520
Shang Zhitao is moving to Alex's team?

162
00:14:41,600 --> 00:14:43,560
Yes. I approved it.

163
00:14:43,640 --> 00:14:45,960
I think she's a good fit for Alex's team.

164
00:14:46,480 --> 00:14:47,840
How is she a good fit?

165
00:14:50,920 --> 00:14:52,040
Bring her back.

166
00:14:52,120 --> 00:14:53,800
I'm used to working with her.

167
00:14:54,720 --> 00:14:55,840
Have you finished your work?

168
00:14:55,920 --> 00:14:57,560
Did you turn in your quarterly report?

169
00:14:57,640 --> 00:15:00,480
Get me your quarterly report in one hour.

170
00:15:00,560 --> 00:15:01,800
One hour?

171
00:15:03,080 --> 00:15:03,920
Why are you still here?

172
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:06,120
No wonder no one wants to work for you.

173
00:15:06,680 --> 00:15:08,120
- Even I want out.
- Fifty minutes.

174
00:15:16,760 --> 00:15:20,160
OK. Before we officially begin,
let's welcome our new colleague.

175
00:15:21,040 --> 00:15:22,560
Introduce yourself.

176
00:15:22,640 --> 00:15:25,320
Hi, everyone. I'm Shang Zhitao.
My English name is Flora.

177
00:15:25,400 --> 00:15:26,560
I'll be joining as an account executive.

178
00:15:26,640 --> 00:15:29,320
Great. Annie will be
your mentor from now on.

179
00:15:29,400 --> 00:15:30,400
You'll be assigning her work.

180
00:15:30,480 --> 00:15:34,320
OK, Flora, please take the minutes
for today's meeting.

181
00:15:34,400 --> 00:15:35,480
Come to me anytime if you have questions.

182
00:15:35,560 --> 00:15:36,760
Got it.

183
00:15:37,400 --> 00:15:39,600
Remember to use the company template
for the minutes.

184
00:15:40,720 --> 00:15:42,600
Don't use the format from your old team.

185
00:15:44,400 --> 00:15:46,360
Annie, bring everyone up to speed
on this case.

186
00:15:46,440 --> 00:15:47,280
Sure.

187
00:15:47,360 --> 00:15:48,760
Could you pull up slide 5?

188
00:15:51,160 --> 00:15:53,680
The key visual for this brief
isn't working for me.

189
00:15:53,760 --> 00:15:56,600
Make it red. Give it more of a party vibe.

190
00:15:56,680 --> 00:15:58,480
The CVR and CTR need revising too.

191
00:15:58,560 --> 00:16:01,400
For the OOA,
I'm aiming for around ten million views.

192
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:04,400
As for the PVG…

193
00:16:11,360 --> 00:16:13,200
All right. If there are no questions,
let's proceed with this plan.

194
00:16:15,560 --> 00:16:18,200
Flora, are you good with Excel?

195
00:16:19,320 --> 00:16:21,600
- Yes.
- I sent you a spreadsheet. Take a look.

196
00:16:22,560 --> 00:16:24,240
Add a column showing the profit or loss

197
00:16:24,320 --> 00:16:26,040
so the client can see
the bottom line at a glance.

198
00:16:26,120 --> 00:16:27,040
OK.

199
00:16:32,760 --> 00:16:35,440
REVENUE, EXPENSES, PROFIT

200
00:16:35,520 --> 00:16:36,920
You know formula shortcuts?

201
00:16:37,920 --> 00:16:39,920
Yes. I taught myself Excel systematically.

202
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:43,600
I was going to ask Finance
to help me make a pivot chart.

203
00:16:43,680 --> 00:16:45,320
- Can you do that?
- Yes.

204
00:16:45,960 --> 00:16:47,360
Can you get it to me
by the end of the day?

205
00:16:48,560 --> 00:16:49,520
No problem.

206
00:17:13,520 --> 00:17:15,640
You're Flora, right? I'm Tianran.

207
00:17:17,240 --> 00:17:19,800
- What are you drinking?
- Barley tea.

208
00:17:21,319 --> 00:17:23,119
No one on our team drinks that.

209
00:17:23,200 --> 00:17:24,760
We all drink black coffee.

210
00:17:24,839 --> 00:17:26,680
It keeps us sharp
and stops us overthinking.

211
00:17:27,960 --> 00:17:30,200
I… I don't like black coffee.

212
00:17:32,720 --> 00:17:33,560
I get it.

213
00:17:34,640 --> 00:17:38,240
I heard you had a pretty rough time
on Luke's team.

214
00:17:38,320 --> 00:17:41,120
It must've been as bitter as this coffee.

215
00:17:41,200 --> 00:17:42,600
Smart move,

216
00:17:42,680 --> 00:17:44,600
jumping from the back burner
onto the fast track.

217
00:17:46,680 --> 00:17:49,240
Luke treated me well.

218
00:17:51,040 --> 00:17:52,360
He treated you well?

219
00:17:54,680 --> 00:17:57,960
I heard he went to war with the company

220
00:17:58,040 --> 00:18:00,480
because one of his subordinates
got hurt on set.

221
00:18:00,560 --> 00:18:01,960
That wasn't you, was it?

222
00:18:02,040 --> 00:18:03,560
Yes, that was me.

223
00:18:05,200 --> 00:18:06,760
Then why did you join our team?

224
00:18:08,920 --> 00:18:09,960
It's work.

225
00:18:10,040 --> 00:18:12,240
At work, don't results matter
more than the process?

226
00:18:15,280 --> 00:18:16,720
You're pretty good with words.

227
00:18:18,120 --> 00:18:19,360
Want to try some?

228
00:18:19,440 --> 00:18:21,280
Barley tea is good for your stomach.

229
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:25,000
I'll get going, then.

230
00:19:04,240 --> 00:19:06,080
MEETING MINUTES

231
00:19:17,840 --> 00:19:20,440
DU ANNI

232
00:19:21,200 --> 00:19:22,280
Annie,

233
00:19:22,360 --> 00:19:24,040
I've emailed you the meeting minutes.

234
00:19:24,120 --> 00:19:26,840
Alex likes to see the minutes
before the end of the workday.

235
00:19:26,920 --> 00:19:28,520
I've finished them
and sent them to everyone.

236
00:19:30,480 --> 00:19:31,400
I'm sorry.

237
00:19:31,480 --> 00:19:33,440
I was too slow. I'll be quicker next time.

238
00:19:34,040 --> 00:19:35,920
You're new,
so I won't blame you this time.

239
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:37,520
But you need to adapt quickly.

240
00:19:38,120 --> 00:19:39,240
And one more thing.

241
00:19:39,320 --> 00:19:42,240
Alex hates it when his people get
too close to colleagues on other teams.

242
00:19:42,320 --> 00:19:44,800
Everything you're working on
must remain strictly confidential.

243
00:19:45,520 --> 00:19:47,760
You need to remember whose team you're on.

244
00:19:48,480 --> 00:19:49,720
Am I making myself clear?

245
00:19:52,080 --> 00:19:53,120
Yes.

246
00:19:53,760 --> 00:19:54,920
Thank you, Annie.

247
00:20:04,840 --> 00:20:05,920
What's wrong?

248
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:07,480
It's only your first day
after the transfer,

249
00:20:07,560 --> 00:20:08,680
and you already look drained.

250
00:20:09,200 --> 00:20:10,040
Things didn't go well?

251
00:20:11,720 --> 00:20:13,400
Ever feel completely out of your depth?

252
00:20:14,120 --> 00:20:16,440
Is it that hard to fit in with the elite?

253
00:20:17,120 --> 00:20:19,120
What exactly is hard?
Is the workload heavy?

254
00:20:21,960 --> 00:20:23,560
My English is terrible.

255
00:20:25,240 --> 00:20:27,520
I couldn't even keep up well enough
to take the meeting minutes.

256
00:20:27,600 --> 00:20:30,360
They used so much industry jargon.
I couldn't understand.

257
00:20:30,440 --> 00:20:32,040
Industry jargon in English?

258
00:20:32,120 --> 00:20:33,800
Ask Long Zhentian
to give you a crash course.

259
00:20:33,880 --> 00:20:36,160
Long Zhentian can't help with this.

260
00:20:36,760 --> 00:20:38,120
I think you can handle it yourself.

261
00:20:39,520 --> 00:20:43,120
Every industry has its own jargon
and technical terms.

262
00:20:43,200 --> 00:20:45,480
When you're just starting out,
all the jargon can be overwhelming,

263
00:20:46,080 --> 00:20:48,400
so it's easy to think the work
is more complicated than it really is.

264
00:20:49,240 --> 00:20:50,400
Write everything down.

265
00:20:50,480 --> 00:20:52,640
Listen, read, and practice more.

266
00:20:52,720 --> 00:20:53,920
In a month,

267
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:55,400
you'll be able to handle it with ease.

268
00:20:55,480 --> 00:20:57,320
A month is too long.

269
00:20:57,400 --> 00:20:59,600
I want to master it in a week.

270
00:21:00,920 --> 00:21:03,160
Tao, one week?

271
00:21:03,240 --> 00:21:05,200
Listen. The whole world's just winging it.

272
00:21:05,920 --> 00:21:07,880
You're being too hard on yourself.

273
00:21:07,960 --> 00:21:10,080
Relax. We're all doing life
for the first time.

274
00:21:11,920 --> 00:21:14,560
Take it one step at a time.
Don't rush. It'll all work out.

275
00:21:18,080 --> 00:21:19,720
How come you have this?

276
00:21:21,720 --> 00:21:23,320
At the book stall
by Peking University's south gate,

277
00:21:23,400 --> 00:21:24,320
books were ten yuan a kilo.

278
00:21:24,400 --> 00:21:26,240
Those are all just fancy words.

279
00:21:26,920 --> 00:21:28,840
Take your time with it.
Ask me if you have any questions.

280
00:21:28,920 --> 00:21:30,920
Zhu, how are you so good at everything?

281
00:21:31,520 --> 00:21:32,720
Ms. Shang.

282
00:21:32,800 --> 00:21:34,080
Working means putting up
with a lot of grief.

283
00:21:34,160 --> 00:21:35,440
Just today,

284
00:21:35,520 --> 00:21:37,880
our accountant told me
I'd exceeded my travel allowance

285
00:21:37,960 --> 00:21:39,560
and had to pay part of it myself.

286
00:21:39,640 --> 00:21:40,480
Isn't that unfair?

287
00:21:40,560 --> 00:21:42,240
Exactly. It's totally unfair.

288
00:21:42,320 --> 00:21:43,400
My boss is the same.

289
00:21:43,480 --> 00:21:47,680
He set my monthly KPI
at 20 successful matches.

290
00:21:47,760 --> 00:21:49,560
Isn't that forcing me
to pair people up at random?

291
00:21:49,640 --> 00:21:50,920
I'm done with it.

292
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:52,520
- Whatever happens, happens.
- Then I'm not traveling for work either.

293
00:21:52,600 --> 00:21:53,760
Whatever happens, happens.

294
00:21:54,720 --> 00:21:56,080
Work's been…

295
00:21:59,360 --> 00:22:00,840
- Go on.
- Say it.

296
00:22:00,920 --> 00:22:02,760
Work's been fine lately.

297
00:22:04,720 --> 00:22:06,160
Yuanzhu, you're not much of a team player.

298
00:22:06,240 --> 00:22:07,560
Sun Yu, take away his chopsticks.

299
00:22:07,640 --> 00:22:09,240
You're not with us.

300
00:22:13,360 --> 00:22:15,440
Fine. Then I won't
go to work tomorrow either.

301
00:22:16,160 --> 00:22:19,600
It's settled. Anyone who goes
to work tomorrow is a corporate lapdog.

302
00:22:19,680 --> 00:22:20,680
Who's a corporate lapdog?

303
00:22:20,760 --> 00:22:22,080
Who's a corporate lapdog?

304
00:22:24,280 --> 00:22:26,240
I have to work tomorrow.

305
00:22:27,440 --> 00:22:28,360
I'm the corporate lapdog.

306
00:22:29,240 --> 00:22:30,280
Get her a dog bowl!

307
00:22:31,120 --> 00:22:32,480
Bark twice, and I'll give you meat.

308
00:22:32,560 --> 00:22:34,000
- I'll get it myself.
- Go ahead.

309
00:22:35,360 --> 00:22:36,440
Pass me some salmon.

310
00:22:36,960 --> 00:22:38,000
I've got dipping sauce here.

311
00:22:38,080 --> 00:22:39,160
Anyone want some?

312
00:22:39,240 --> 00:22:40,160
- I'll take some.
- I refuse sauce offered in contempt.

313
00:22:40,240 --> 00:22:41,400
I'll take some from you.

314
00:22:41,480 --> 00:22:42,720
Do you want some or not?

315
00:22:42,800 --> 00:22:45,000
Fish balls, anyone? Do you want some?

316
00:22:50,680 --> 00:22:51,440
QIPAI JEWELRY

317
00:22:51,520 --> 00:22:52,720
We're really sorry.

318
00:22:52,800 --> 00:22:55,840
We'll revise the proposal
and get you an updated version ASAP.

319
00:22:55,920 --> 00:22:57,160
- We'll make sure you're satisfied.
- Don't bother.

320
00:22:57,880 --> 00:23:00,720
I don't think the result will be any good.

321
00:23:00,800 --> 00:23:04,640
Every revised version you've submitted
is even worse than Luke's first draft.

322
00:23:05,200 --> 00:23:06,560
Let me be direct.

323
00:23:06,640 --> 00:23:10,080
We want to go back
to Luke's original proposal.

324
00:23:17,400 --> 00:23:20,600
They want a rock-bottom price
and Luke's original proposal?

325
00:23:20,680 --> 00:23:21,800
They can't have it both ways.

326
00:23:22,480 --> 00:23:23,640
Exactly.

327
00:23:24,160 --> 00:23:25,400
And you know Luke's temper.

328
00:23:25,480 --> 00:23:27,600
Last time, when Lucy asked for some data,

329
00:23:27,680 --> 00:23:29,880
Lumi bit her head off.

330
00:23:29,960 --> 00:23:32,280
Luan Nian's proposal belongs to Lime.

331
00:23:33,360 --> 00:23:35,200
The project is with our team now.

332
00:23:35,280 --> 00:23:36,960
If he refuses to cooperate,

333
00:23:37,560 --> 00:23:38,880
he'll be costing the company the project.

334
00:23:42,120 --> 00:23:44,160
Flora used to be on Luke's team.

335
00:23:44,240 --> 00:23:45,440
She gets along with him.

336
00:23:45,520 --> 00:23:47,680
Why don't we let her try?

337
00:23:53,720 --> 00:23:54,840
She's new.

338
00:23:54,920 --> 00:23:55,920
She needs to see the bigger picture.

339
00:23:56,600 --> 00:23:58,240
When she delivers the files later,

340
00:23:58,920 --> 00:24:01,000
remind her to compliment Luke's new tie.

341
00:24:09,080 --> 00:24:12,280
Most people in the company
are too intimidated to talk to Luke.

342
00:24:12,800 --> 00:24:15,200
But Li Tianran said
you two got along well.

343
00:24:15,280 --> 00:24:16,880
Now that you're on our team,

344
00:24:17,920 --> 00:24:19,400
it's time to put that connection to use.

345
00:24:24,360 --> 00:24:25,320
We'll leave it there.

346
00:24:26,760 --> 00:24:27,600
Come in.

347
00:24:32,360 --> 00:24:33,400
Luke.

348
00:24:47,120 --> 00:24:50,480
The client from Qipai
wants to use the previous proposal.

349
00:24:51,120 --> 00:24:54,720
Could you share the source files with us?

350
00:24:59,080 --> 00:25:00,640
Did you volunteer to come,

351
00:25:01,240 --> 00:25:02,680
or did Alex send you?

352
00:25:03,760 --> 00:25:04,920
I was assigned this task.

353
00:25:07,640 --> 00:25:11,120
Did you transfer just to become
their pawn against me?

354
00:25:12,960 --> 00:25:14,240
You're reading too much into this.

355
00:25:14,320 --> 00:25:15,400
No one's out to get you.

356
00:25:17,280 --> 00:25:19,000
When Alex took you onto his team,

357
00:25:19,080 --> 00:25:20,120
didn't he make you prove your loyalty?

358
00:25:24,920 --> 00:25:27,360
Every supervisor wants loyal subordinates.

359
00:25:27,440 --> 00:25:29,360
When you were my supervisor,
I was loyal to you too.

360
00:25:31,320 --> 00:25:32,160
Fine.

361
00:25:32,240 --> 00:25:34,880
Go back and tell him
I won't give them to you.

362
00:25:34,960 --> 00:25:36,280
What do you think he'll say?

363
00:25:38,960 --> 00:25:40,720
Probably the same thing you did.

364
00:25:41,480 --> 00:25:42,880
He'll want me to quit.

365
00:25:44,760 --> 00:25:46,720
You don't have to quit.
Come back to our team.

366
00:25:47,560 --> 00:25:49,320
I'm willing to take you back,
despite everything.

367
00:25:49,920 --> 00:25:52,000
At least when it comes
to professional ethics,

368
00:25:52,080 --> 00:25:53,960
you meet my standards.

369
00:25:59,640 --> 00:26:00,720
You're a senior executive.

370
00:26:00,800 --> 00:26:02,000
You see the bigger picture.

371
00:26:02,720 --> 00:26:05,360
You can contact me anytime
if you change your mind.

372
00:26:07,360 --> 00:26:08,840
I'm not that magnanimous.

373
00:26:10,320 --> 00:26:12,480
Unlike you, I know right from wrong.

374
00:26:14,480 --> 00:26:15,720
You want the source files?

375
00:26:16,320 --> 00:26:17,440
Then wait.

376
00:26:20,680 --> 00:26:21,640
Close the door behind you.

377
00:26:31,720 --> 00:26:32,760
Stubborn.

378
00:26:34,440 --> 00:26:36,040
You want the source files
for our proposal?

379
00:26:37,000 --> 00:26:38,040
Have you no shame?

380
00:26:38,120 --> 00:26:39,880
We're just making the best use
of company resources.

381
00:26:40,680 --> 00:26:41,600
We all work for Lime.

382
00:26:41,680 --> 00:26:43,520
Besides, we wouldn't
be asking for your help

383
00:26:43,600 --> 00:26:45,600
if the client hadn't asked for them.

384
00:26:45,680 --> 00:26:46,760
Then don't bother asking.

385
00:26:47,360 --> 00:26:51,240
You were capable enough to take
the Qipai project from us.

386
00:26:52,360 --> 00:26:55,160
Surely you're capable enough
to handle it yourselves.

387
00:26:58,320 --> 00:27:00,160
And now you have the nerve
to ask us for the files?

388
00:27:00,240 --> 00:27:03,400
Didn't your mother teach you that thieves
get what's coming to them?

389
00:27:05,080 --> 00:27:06,280
Keep up the good work.

390
00:27:08,440 --> 00:27:10,480
This is an office,
not your neighborhood market.

391
00:27:10,560 --> 00:27:11,680
We're all colleagues.

392
00:27:11,760 --> 00:27:13,240
Watch your mouth.

393
00:27:14,280 --> 00:27:16,000
A vicious dog always gets
what's coming to it.

394
00:27:16,080 --> 00:27:17,880
Enjoy your little win while it lasts.

395
00:27:17,960 --> 00:27:19,560
Have some dignity, will you?

396
00:27:19,640 --> 00:27:21,000
Come looking for trouble again,

397
00:27:21,800 --> 00:27:23,080
and you'll regret it.

398
00:27:23,160 --> 00:27:24,280
Get lost.

399
00:27:30,720 --> 00:27:32,080
Send me the files.

400
00:27:46,200 --> 00:27:47,040
Is this for me?

401
00:27:47,560 --> 00:27:48,640
Thanks.

402
00:27:50,920 --> 00:27:52,040
Lumi,

403
00:27:53,040 --> 00:27:54,960
I didn't know switching teams
would cause all this.

404
00:27:55,040 --> 00:27:57,400
And I had no idea
that things were so tense

405
00:27:58,240 --> 00:27:59,200
between you and Alex's team.

406
00:27:59,280 --> 00:28:01,680
Had I known--

407
00:28:01,760 --> 00:28:04,960
You haven't been here long enough
to know all the bad blood between us.

408
00:28:05,040 --> 00:28:07,080
This company is full
of competing interests.

409
00:28:07,160 --> 00:28:08,920
Taking sides is unavoidable.

410
00:28:11,400 --> 00:28:13,720
You don't need to feel guilty.

411
00:28:13,800 --> 00:28:15,320
Just focus on your own work.

412
00:28:15,840 --> 00:28:18,760
They gave me an impossible task.

413
00:28:22,600 --> 00:28:25,240
They told you to ask Luke
for the source files?

414
00:28:26,760 --> 00:28:27,880
Damn it.

415
00:28:28,760 --> 00:28:30,120
They really know how to pick
an easy target.

416
00:28:32,520 --> 00:28:33,960
I can't help you with this.

417
00:28:34,040 --> 00:28:35,480
Luke always keeps
the source files himself.

418
00:28:35,560 --> 00:28:36,400
They never pass through me.

419
00:28:37,200 --> 00:28:38,360
My advice?

420
00:28:38,440 --> 00:28:41,280
Turn this task down,
or it could blow up in your face.

421
00:28:43,000 --> 00:28:44,480
I… I understand.

422
00:28:46,240 --> 00:28:50,560
Save this cake for the kids.

423
00:29:08,600 --> 00:29:10,840
DU ANNI: REPORT BACK BY TOMORROW

424
00:29:15,000 --> 00:29:16,480
LINGDONG SQUASH CENTER

425
00:29:16,560 --> 00:29:18,280
He broke the rules first,

426
00:29:18,360 --> 00:29:20,160
so there's nothing wrong
with you venting a little.

427
00:29:21,160 --> 00:29:24,360
Bottling it all up
isn't good for your health.

428
00:29:25,200 --> 00:29:28,120
And this will help
set things straight at Lime.

429
00:29:30,440 --> 00:29:32,040
Are you here to back Alex up, Mr. Lin?

430
00:29:33,520 --> 00:29:34,560
I'm not taking anyone's side.

431
00:29:34,640 --> 00:29:35,880
I'm only thinking of Lime.

432
00:29:36,400 --> 00:29:37,760
Don't worry.

433
00:29:37,840 --> 00:29:39,600
Wherever the Qipai project goes,

434
00:29:39,680 --> 00:29:40,880
it'll stay within Lime.

435
00:29:40,960 --> 00:29:41,880
We won't lose it.

436
00:29:43,800 --> 00:29:44,680
Good.

437
00:29:45,200 --> 00:29:48,720
And I never shortchange
employees who see the bigger picture.

438
00:29:49,240 --> 00:29:51,520
There's an awards ceremony next week.
Come with me.

439
00:29:51,600 --> 00:29:55,040
I'll give you projects from several
of Lime's longtime clients.

440
00:29:55,120 --> 00:29:56,600
They'll be every bit as good as Qipai.

441
00:29:57,440 --> 00:29:59,880
- OK.
- Want to grab a drink afterward?

442
00:30:05,920 --> 00:30:06,760
TAOBAO

443
00:30:06,840 --> 00:30:08,560
- Hello. Your food delivery.
- Thanks.

444
00:30:17,800 --> 00:30:18,960
What's wrong?

445
00:30:19,040 --> 00:30:20,840
Why are you taking it out on that radish?

446
00:30:22,000 --> 00:30:23,280
I don't think

447
00:30:24,480 --> 00:30:26,800
I can keep doing this job.

448
00:30:26,880 --> 00:30:30,800
My boss wants me to get the files
from Luan Nian

449
00:30:30,880 --> 00:30:34,400
to prove my worth to the new team.

450
00:30:37,560 --> 00:30:38,520
Let me ask you this.

451
00:30:39,040 --> 00:30:40,600
Do you still want to stay at Lime?

452
00:30:42,800 --> 00:30:43,920
Of course I do.

453
00:30:44,000 --> 00:30:45,400
Then there's your answer.

454
00:30:45,480 --> 00:30:48,240
Aren't you two back
to a normal working relationship now?

455
00:30:48,840 --> 00:30:52,520
Asking him for a file
is a perfectly normal work interaction.

456
00:30:53,280 --> 00:30:54,160
Tao,

457
00:30:54,880 --> 00:30:57,520
stop questioning yourself
and overthinking everything.

458
00:30:57,600 --> 00:31:02,080
What you should be figuring out now
is how to get the files

459
00:31:02,760 --> 00:31:03,920
and finish your job.

460
00:31:09,720 --> 00:31:10,720
You're right.

461
00:31:14,000 --> 00:31:15,160
Right.

462
00:31:24,160 --> 00:31:27,880
You need to remember whose team you're on.

463
00:31:27,960 --> 00:31:30,360
Fine. Go back and tell him

464
00:31:30,440 --> 00:31:31,840
I won't give them to you.

465
00:31:31,920 --> 00:31:33,000
What do you think he'll say?

466
00:31:33,880 --> 00:31:35,600
Probably the same thing you did.

467
00:31:35,680 --> 00:31:36,880
He'll want me to quit.

468
00:31:48,360 --> 00:31:49,360
Luke.

469
00:31:49,880 --> 00:31:53,280
I apologize for how I acted
this afternoon,

470
00:31:53,840 --> 00:31:55,760
but I really need the source files.

471
00:31:55,840 --> 00:31:57,240
I know this isn't right,

472
00:31:57,320 --> 00:31:58,960
- but could you…?
- Shang Zhitao.

473
00:32:01,320 --> 00:32:02,240
Enter the code for me.

474
00:32:15,160 --> 00:32:16,360
What is it?

475
00:32:17,080 --> 00:32:18,200
Seven-zero-eight-zero-zero.

476
00:32:22,320 --> 00:32:24,600
Verified. Please open the door.

477
00:33:08,320 --> 00:33:09,520
Shang Zhitao.

478
00:33:20,200 --> 00:33:21,560
What are you doing?

479
00:33:27,920 --> 00:33:28,760
Luke.

480
00:33:29,800 --> 00:33:30,760
Don't talk.

481
00:33:59,080 --> 00:34:01,080
After alcohol hits,

482
00:34:01,160 --> 00:34:04,600
there's usually a half-hour
transition period.

483
00:34:05,160 --> 00:34:06,680
During that half hour,

484
00:34:07,320 --> 00:34:11,840
everything a person does
is a mix of reason and confusion.

485
00:34:12,600 --> 00:34:16,000
At times like this,
anyone of the opposite sex

486
00:34:16,600 --> 00:34:18,199
looks more attractive than usual.

487
00:34:19,080 --> 00:34:20,239
He's just drunk.

488
00:34:46,760 --> 00:34:47,960
Shang Zhitao.

489
00:34:53,719 --> 00:34:54,679
You're awake.

490
00:34:57,680 --> 00:34:59,000
You stayed here all night?

491
00:35:00,040 --> 00:35:01,640
I was going to leave yesterday,

492
00:35:02,360 --> 00:35:03,880
but then you threw up.

493
00:35:03,960 --> 00:35:05,480
I was worried something
might happen to you.

494
00:35:05,560 --> 00:35:07,000
Plus,

495
00:35:07,080 --> 00:35:09,040
I'd been up dealing with you all night
and was exhausted,

496
00:35:09,120 --> 00:35:09,960
so I fell asleep.

497
00:35:10,560 --> 00:35:11,520
Did you change my clothes?

498
00:35:12,680 --> 00:35:14,880
Yes. You threw up all over yourself
last night,

499
00:35:14,960 --> 00:35:16,000
so I changed them for you.

500
00:35:16,600 --> 00:35:18,120
Then I washed both our clothes.

501
00:35:18,720 --> 00:35:19,760
Don't get the wrong idea.

502
00:35:21,600 --> 00:35:22,560
Fine.

503
00:35:23,120 --> 00:35:24,400
- I'm going to take a shower.
- Luke,

504
00:35:25,240 --> 00:35:26,080
the previous proposal…

505
00:36:16,520 --> 00:36:19,600
The client from Qipai
wants to use the previous proposal.

506
00:36:20,240 --> 00:36:23,840
Could you share the source files with us?

507
00:36:24,840 --> 00:36:27,000
But I really need the source files.

508
00:36:44,560 --> 00:36:45,400
Hello?

509
00:36:46,040 --> 00:36:47,240
Where are you?

510
00:36:47,320 --> 00:36:49,160
I'm on my way to the bus stop.

511
00:36:51,000 --> 00:36:52,200
Come back now.

512
00:36:54,760 --> 00:36:56,160
- Now?
- Now.

513
00:36:58,000 --> 00:36:59,040
I can't.

514
00:36:59,120 --> 00:37:01,040
I need to go home and get ready,

515
00:37:01,120 --> 00:37:02,720
- then head to the office--
- Come back now.

516
00:37:02,800 --> 00:37:04,240
Something's missing from my place.

517
00:37:24,120 --> 00:37:25,040
Sorry.

518
00:37:25,120 --> 00:37:27,560
It was chilly when I left,

519
00:37:27,640 --> 00:37:29,480
and my clothes were still wet,

520
00:37:29,560 --> 00:37:31,080
so I borrowed one of your coats.

521
00:37:31,160 --> 00:37:32,880
If you don't want to lend it to me,

522
00:37:32,960 --> 00:37:34,800
I'll take it off right now.

523
00:37:34,880 --> 00:37:36,160
That's not what's missing.

524
00:37:36,800 --> 00:37:39,320
Then, what is?

525
00:37:39,400 --> 00:37:40,960
My safe was broken into.

526
00:37:41,480 --> 00:37:42,600
The diamond is gone.

527
00:37:42,680 --> 00:37:45,680
I don't even know where your safe is.

528
00:37:48,800 --> 00:37:50,080
You must have security cameras.

529
00:37:50,160 --> 00:37:51,880
Why don't we check the footage?

530
00:37:54,800 --> 00:37:57,000
I'm kidding. Come in.

531
00:37:59,200 --> 00:38:02,000
- I need to shower before going to work.
- Why are you in such a rush?

532
00:38:02,520 --> 00:38:03,800
Have you finished your assignment?

533
00:38:07,800 --> 00:38:08,720
Did you bring the USB drive?

534
00:38:14,840 --> 00:38:16,440
ENGLISH-CHINESE &amp;
CHINESE-ENGLISH ADVERTISING TERMINOLOGY

535
00:38:18,520 --> 00:38:20,000
Still brushing up on your English?

536
00:38:20,080 --> 00:38:21,480
Worried Lime will fire you,

537
00:38:22,000 --> 00:38:23,120
and you won't find a better job?

538
00:38:25,120 --> 00:38:26,000
Here it is.

539
00:38:49,800 --> 00:38:51,600
The source files for the Qipai project?

540
00:38:52,280 --> 00:38:53,240
Sit down and wait.

541
00:38:53,760 --> 00:38:54,680
The files are huge.

542
00:38:55,320 --> 00:38:56,600
It'll take 40 minutes to copy them.

543
00:38:59,920 --> 00:39:01,080
Thank you, Luke.

544
00:39:01,160 --> 00:39:02,800
Thank you so, so much.

545
00:39:03,320 --> 00:39:04,160
I'll wait outside.

546
00:39:04,960 --> 00:39:08,080
Will waiting outside
make the transfer any faster?

547
00:39:08,960 --> 00:39:10,400
If you want them, don't chicken out.

548
00:39:18,640 --> 00:39:21,320
You can make slides, right?
Format a deck for me.

549
00:39:21,400 --> 00:39:23,880
I want the final version by 10 a.m.

550
00:39:24,680 --> 00:39:26,200
Sure. I can do that.

551
00:39:56,240 --> 00:39:58,960
The clothes from last night are dry now.

552
00:39:59,040 --> 00:40:00,120
Go shower in the guest room.

553
00:40:00,840 --> 00:40:01,720
Then eat breakfast before you leave.

554
00:40:02,960 --> 00:40:03,800
It's all right.

555
00:40:03,880 --> 00:40:05,240
It's not like you haven't
showered here before.

556
00:40:07,320 --> 00:40:08,760
Do you want to go to work smelling awful?

557
00:40:10,360 --> 00:40:12,320
OK, I… I'll go shower now.

558
00:40:22,840 --> 00:40:23,960
Can you drive?

559
00:40:25,600 --> 00:40:26,440
No.

560
00:40:26,520 --> 00:40:27,480
You can't?

561
00:40:28,400 --> 00:40:29,600
If you collect seven things you can't do,

562
00:40:29,680 --> 00:40:31,120
will Shenron grant you a promotion?

563
00:40:32,160 --> 00:40:35,720
Do you need to pass a driving test
to get promoted at Lime?

564
00:40:36,480 --> 00:40:38,760
Not for promotion,
but you need to drive for the job.

565
00:40:39,840 --> 00:40:40,800
Can't you drive today?

566
00:40:41,960 --> 00:40:43,480
The alcohol hasn't fully metabolized yet.

567
00:40:43,560 --> 00:40:44,400
It'd count as drunk driving.

568
00:40:46,560 --> 00:40:48,240
I'll get a cab. We'll go together.

569
00:40:50,920 --> 00:40:51,920
All right.

570
00:41:02,480 --> 00:41:04,000
YUETENG AUTO INTRODUCTION

571
00:41:04,080 --> 00:41:05,040
YUETENG 5.0 CHURN ANALYSIS

572
00:41:05,120 --> 00:41:06,720
YUETENG 5.0 TARGET USER PROFILE

573
00:41:11,040 --> 00:41:12,280
How is it?

574
00:41:18,080 --> 00:41:19,760
The gold should be glaring like this,

575
00:41:19,840 --> 00:41:22,200
like a car hood baking in the summer sun.

576
00:41:22,280 --> 00:41:23,920
Don't use cheap phrases
like "value for money" in the title.

577
00:41:24,000 --> 00:41:25,960
Focus on how it elevates
the owner's status.

578
00:41:26,040 --> 00:41:27,920
Isn't that a little over the top?

579
00:41:28,000 --> 00:41:30,320
Advertising is all about being
over the top.

580
00:41:30,400 --> 00:41:32,160
Learn from competing proposals.

581
00:41:32,920 --> 00:41:35,600
This was last year's winning campaign,
done in laser gold.

582
00:41:35,680 --> 00:41:36,480
CORE STRATEGY
BROAD REACH, FAST IGNITION

583
00:41:42,000 --> 00:41:43,280
Go learn to drive.

584
00:41:44,360 --> 00:41:46,360
A driver's license is a must at Lime.

585
00:41:46,440 --> 00:41:48,840
Auto brand campaigns
make up over half of Lime's revenue.

586
00:41:48,920 --> 00:41:50,560
Without knowing how to drive,

587
00:41:50,640 --> 00:41:52,240
you can't even gain proper
customer insight.

588
00:41:52,880 --> 00:41:54,960
Even if I could drive,
I still wouldn't have a car.

589
00:41:55,640 --> 00:41:57,360
If you never learn to drive,
you'll never have one.

590
00:42:06,000 --> 00:42:07,040
Luke,

591
00:42:08,560 --> 00:42:10,120
could you let me get out first
when we get there?

592
00:42:12,440 --> 00:42:14,240
Is it embarrassing to be seen with me?

593
00:42:15,440 --> 00:42:16,520
No, it's not.

594
00:42:17,520 --> 00:42:20,480
I just don't want
any unnecessary misunderstandings.

595
00:42:21,800 --> 00:42:23,760
You dared to come to my place
for the files,

596
00:42:23,840 --> 00:42:26,080
but you're afraid of gossip
over sharing a ride?

597
00:42:49,320 --> 00:42:50,560
Get out.

598
00:43:10,720 --> 00:43:12,320
Not bad.

599
00:43:17,600 --> 00:43:19,520
So you really are on good terms with Luke.

600
00:43:45,960 --> 00:43:46,800
Hello.

601
00:43:52,800 --> 00:43:53,880
- Thanks.
- Go ahead.

602
00:44:07,000 --> 00:44:09,080
- Luke, our…
- Shang Zhitao.

603
00:44:11,440 --> 00:44:12,600
Enter the code for me.

604
00:44:14,680 --> 00:44:15,800
Seven-zero-eight-zero-zero.

605
00:44:25,560 --> 00:44:27,880
- Verification failed.
- What was it?

606
00:44:36,040 --> 00:44:38,320
Verified. Please open the door.
